# Implement bounded page texture and soft noise

## Scope and existing evidence

Historical implementation evidence covers typed structures only, unless
explicitly stated otherwise; the finite contract is not rendered output.

Apply seeded low-frequency texture at declared physical scale and prove it does
not move geometry, obscure small writing, or create repeated tiles.

Current executable evidence now freezes page-level texture intent without
generating pixels. A plan retains read-only vector-geometry authority, physical
page bounds, caller-owned physical noise scale, a bounded strength envelope, and
the complete stochastic replay key reused by material layers. Strength validates
inside its inclusive envelope before generation, and successful validation now
returns constructor-sealed evidence borrowing the exact plan.

An exhaustive 343-case integer oracle covers every minimum/maximum/selected
triple in `[-3, 3]` and requires both direct and sealed admission to preserve
inverted-envelope-before-selected-value precedence. Frequency models, texture
generation, tile detection, legibility thresholds, units, rasterization, and
visual evaluation remain open.

## Finite seeded paper texture with an exact off mode

**Inputs:** one immutable vector page, physical paper dimensions, accepted
document seed, material preset, physical noise scale and bounded amplitude.
**Outputs:** a proposed page-background texture field or a refused
out-of-envelope plan. Texture cannot move vectors, alter stroke contact,
obscure text or change physical page boxes.

**Physical-scale policy:** for one A4 page define a low-frequency field with
4 mm correlation length in page millimeters. The default `Off` choice has
zero field and zero additional sampling cost. `Soft` admits luminance delta
up to 1% absolute; `Visible` admits up to 2% when measured contrast remains
above the approved readability bound.

Both are evaluated at a fixed physical
coordinate system independent of zoom or raster output DPI. The declared
variation strength is inclusive within a caller-owned admitted range.

**Worked example:** page `p1`, source seed `doc-42`, preset `paper-soft`
selects `Soft`, 4 mm physical scale and maximum 0.01 luminance shift. At page
coordinate `(25,30) mm`, the same keyed procedural sample must be identical
in Preview and Final; only sampling density changes. A switch to `Off`
returns uniform paper white without touching the `t1` text path or changing
its source/semantic provenance. Independent page identity and position keep
repeated printable tiles from being byte-repeated by mistake.

**Safety limits:** prove texture does not alter source vector coordinates by
treating the geometry authority as read-only and clipping the texture to
paper background. A readability observation must cover the smallest text
role and relevant contrast; absent measurement returns `UnverifiedContrast`
and disables the stronger mode. Tile repetition is a separately reported
quality risk, not assumed absent just because a seed exists.

**Refusal example:** a requested amplitude of 5%, negative physical scale,
reused stochastic key across incompatible pages, or no contrast observation
for `Visible` refuses the effect or falls back to `Off` only with explicit
user choice. Never claim empirical paper realism without photographed paper
data. Unsupported live material effects remain unavailable to a single pen.

**Assumptions and limits:** page texture plans already preserve vector
identity, physical scale, replay key and inclusive amplitude bounds. Actual
noise frequency model, pixel evaluation, tile-detection algorithm, contrast
testing and page rendering remain open. The two amplitudes are theoretical
modes, not measured visual evidence.

## Acceptance decision

- **Basis:** practical for bounded texture intent; theoretical for sampled
  pixels, contrast and repeat detection, 2026-11-02.
- **Delivered:** `Off`/`Soft`/`Visible` at fixed scale, two amplitudes,
  deterministic sample example and explicit unverified/invalid refusals.
- **Not implemented by this acceptance:** generated page noise,
  texture compositing, real contrast scoring or tile artifact detection.
